Nova's decks (slide decks the Muse authors, the deck viewer, and the PowerPoint and PDF export)
contain portions modified from Open Design (https://github.com/nexu-io/open-design, commit
802708f), Copyright the Open Design authors, licensed under the Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE).
Each ported file carries a "Portions modified from nexu-io/open-design <path>@802708f,
Apache-2.0; changes: ..." header naming its source file and what changed:
apps/desktop/src/main/deck-capture.ts and pdf-export.ts (the page-side export logic and print
rules, infra/sandboxes/computer/deck-export/deck-capture-page.js and nova-deck-export),
apps/desktop/tests/main/pptx-editable-fidelity, pptx-layered-background and pptx-cjk-typeface
tests (infra/sandboxes/computer/deck-export/*.test.ts), and packages/contracts/src/prompts/
deck-framework.ts with runtime/deck-protocol.ts (the deck skeleton and navigation protocol,
engine/omnigent/omnigent/superchat/decks/kit/skeleton.html).

Deck editing on the canvas ports ideas and code from Open Design's edit mode, also Apache-2.0
at commit 802708f: apps/web/src/edit-mode/bridge.ts (the in-frame selection, inline text edit and
hover logic, rewritten as apps/web/src/features/decks/edit/bridge.js), apps/web/src/edit-mode/
source-patches.ts (the patch kinds, rewritten in Python as engine/omnigent/omnigent/superchat/
decks/patches.py), the manual edit panel (rewritten small as StylePanel.tsx), and the
attached-preview-comments block (deck-ask.ts). The untrusted-text sanitizer comes from this
repository's Omnigent web client (engine/omnigent/web/src/lib/designModePrompt.ts).

The PowerPoint export vendors dom-to-pptx 2.0.1 (https://github.com/atharva9167j/dom-to-pptx),
MIT License, Copyright (c) 2025 Atharva Dharmendra Jagtap and dom-to-pptx contributors, as the
browser bundle Open Design ships; its license is kept in
infra/sandboxes/computer/deck-export/vendor/dom-to-pptx/LICENSE.

Charts in HTML decks. The chart slide recipes (engine/omnigent/omnigent/superchat/decks/kit/charts)
are the chart-bar, chart-line, chart-pie and chart-radar slides of Open Design's html-ppt
design template (design-templates/html-ppt/templates/single-page, commit 802708f), MIT, Copyright
(c) 2026 lewis (charts/LICENSE-html-ppt), plus the fixed-height chart container rule of its
skills/data-report skill; each recipe carries its "Portions modified from" header. They draw with
Chart.js 4.4.3 (MIT, Copyright (c) 2014-2024 Chart.js Contributors), vendored unchanged in
engine/omnigent/omnigent/superchat/decks/kit/vendor/chart.js. The PowerPoint export reads each
Chart.js chart and writes a native chart through a small patch to the vendored dom-to-pptx
(infra/sandboxes/computer/deck-export/vendor/dom-to-pptx/README.md). The native-object test helper
(engine/omnigent/tests/superchat/decks/pptx_native.py) is ported from Open Design's humanize-ppt
plugin (plugins/community/humanize-ppt/scripts/pptx_qa.py, commit 802708f), MIT, Copyright (c) 2026
LearnPrompt.

Dashboards. The dashboard page template (infra/sandboxes/computer/dashboard/template.html), which
nova-dashboard fills from the person's files, is modified from Open Design's data-report skill
(skills/data-report/example.html, commit 802708f), Apache-2.0, and carries its "Portions modified
from" header: the report header, the KPI cards with a sparkline and change, the chart grid with its
fixed-height chart boxes and the data table. It inlines the same vendored Chart.js 4.4.3 (MIT) as
the decks.

The deck themes (engine/omnigent/omnigent/superchat/decks/kit/templates, 18 of them) are rewritten
from MIT-licensed Open Design design templates, each keeping its LICENSE file beside the theme and a
"Design derived from ..." header in its theme.css. From zarazhangrui/beautiful-html-templates
(Copyright (c) 2026 Zara Zhang): Blue Professional, Editorial Tri-Tone, Cartesian. From
lewislulu/html-ppt-skill (Copyright (c) 2026 lewis), as shipped in Open Design's html-ppt template
at 802708f: Corporate Clean, Minimal White, Swiss Grid, Arctic Cool, Academic Paper, Editorial Serif,
Japanese Minimal, Magazine Bold, Bauhaus, Midcentury, Pitch Deck VC, Sharp Mono, Nord and Tokyo
Night. From op7418/guizang-ppt-skill (Copyright (c) 2026 op7418): Magazine Mono. Gradients and
shadows were dropped so every theme exports to native PowerPoint shapes. The Nord theme uses the Nord
palette (Arctic Ice Studio, Copyright (c) 2016-present Sven Greb, MIT) and the Tokyo Night theme the
Tokyo Night palette (enkia, Copyright (c) 2018 enkia, MIT). Their fonts
(kit/fonts) are Latin subsets of Space Grotesk, Inter, Bricolage Grotesque, Instrument Serif,
JetBrains Mono, Newsreader, Playfair Display and Archivo Black, each under the SIL Open Font
License 1.1 with its license text (OFL-*.txt) beside the font files.

The native PowerPoint skill (infra/sandboxes/computer/pptx/skill/pptx-generator) is a port of the
pptx-generator skill from MiniMax-AI/skills (https://github.com/MiniMax-AI/skills, commit
60aaae52bb2af8162732751a4332f62a5fef518b, path skills/pptx-generator), Copyright (c) 2026 MiniMax,
licensed under the MIT License; the license text is kept beside the skill in
infra/sandboxes/computer/pptx/skill/pptx-generator/LICENSE. Each ported file carries a "Portions
from MiniMax-AI/skills <path>@60aaae5, MIT; changes: ..." header. The Computer image installs
PptxGenJS 4.0.1 (MIT, Copyright (c) Brent Ely), react, react-dom, react-icons, sharp, python-pptx
and markitdown for it, each under its own permissive license, and applies the upstream PptxGenJS
fixes for gitbrent/PptxGenJS issue 1531 and pull requests 1537 and 1540
(infra/sandboxes/computer/pptx/runtime/patches).

Two small chat behaviors port ideas and wording from nao (https://github.com/getnao/nao, Copyright
2025 nao Labs, commit 5bde830), Apache-2.0 (see LICENSE); only files without the "@license
Enterprise" header were used. Each ported file carries a "Portions modified from getnao/nao
<path>@5bde830, Apache-2.0; changes: ..." header:
engine/omnigent/omnigent/superchat/cards/tools.py (the `ask_clarification` and `suggest_follow_ups`
tools, from apps/shared/src/tools/clarification.ts and suggest-follow-ups.ts; they emit Nova's reply
cards instead of nao's tool-call UI), and the memory extraction rules in
engine/omnigent/omnigent/memory/upkeep.py, engine/omnigent/omnigent/superchat/daily_notes/
quiet_moment.py and infra/omnigent/templates/AGENTS.md (from apps/backend/src/components/ai/
memory-system-prompt.tsx and agents/memory/memory-extractor-llm.ts: standing instructions apart
from profile facts, instructions gated on permanence signals, supersede on change). Nova's
recurring-task support (the Muse writes the RRULE, the server validates it and previews the next
fire times) is its own design: nao's cron-nlp.ts was read for the idea only and no code or prompt
from it is used.

Nova's file-search guidance (the "The person's files" section of infra/omnigent/templates/AGENTS.md)
and the shape of its files_* tools (search by keywords, by meaning, hybrid with a model rerank; get
and multi-get; status) are adapted from the pi-qmd extension and its qmd-knowledge skill
(https://github.com/hjanuschka/pi-qmd, commit 8266056, skills/qmd-knowledge/SKILL.md), Copyright (c)
hjanuschka, licensed under the MIT License (declared in its package.json and README; the repository
ships no separate LICENSE file), which wraps qmd (https://github.com/tobi/qmd, MIT, Copyright (c)
Tobi Lutke). No qmd or pi-qmd code is included: the tools are re-implemented in Python over SQLite
FTS5 and sqlite-vec (omnigent/runner/knowledge).

Charts. The chart capability (packages/charts, engine/omnigent/omnigent/superchat/charts,
apps/api/src/features/charts, apps/web/src/features/charts) contains portions modified from nao
(https://github.com/getnao/nao, commit 5bde830), Copyright 2025 nao Labs, licensed under the Apache
License 2.0 (see LICENSE); files under nao's `@license Enterprise` headers were not used. Each ported
file carries a "Portions modified from getnao/nao <path>@5bde830, Apache-2.0; changes: ..." header:
apps/shared/src/tools/display-chart.ts (the chart spec and its model-facing descriptions, ported to
zod 4 in packages/charts/src/spec.ts and to pydantic in engine/.../charts/spec.py),
apps/shared/src/chart-builder.tsx, chart-tooltip.tsx, chart-data-labels.tsx, chart-values.ts,
chart-domain.ts, date.ts, chart-types.ts, chart-fonts.ts,
chart-style.ts and class-names.ts (packages/charts/src), and apps/backend/src/components/generate-chart.tsx
with utils/generate-chart.ts (the server-side SVG and PNG render, apps/api/src/features/charts/render.ts
and packages/charts/src/prepare.tsx).

The charts depend on recharts 2.15.4 (MIT), d3-format 3.1.0 (ISC) and, for the
server-side PNG, @resvg/resvg-js 2.6.2 (Mozilla Public License 2.0, https://github.com/yisibl/resvg-js),
used unmodified as a library; no MPL-licensed source file is copied into or modified by this repository.

The server-side chart PNGs are drawn with the DejaVu Sans and DejaVu Sans Bold fonts
(apps/api/assets/fonts, copied from nao's apps/backend/assets/fonts), (c) Bitstream, Inc. and Tavmjong
Bah, DejaVu changes in the public domain, under the Bitstream Vera / DejaVu font license kept beside the
fonts in apps/api/assets/fonts/LICENSE-DejaVu.txt.
